cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KUKA KR 6 R900 sixx — Complete Kinematics Suite"
message: "If you use this software in academic or industrial work, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Janga
    given-names: Bliss
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch implementation of forward and inverse kinematics, the
  geometric Jacobian, singularity diagnostics, and joint- and task-space
  trajectory planning for the KUKA KR 6 R900 sixx six-degree-of-freedom
  industrial manipulator. Includes a programmatically generated URDF whose
  link frames coincide with the analytic DH frames, and a verification
  test-suite that checks the implementation against the manufacturer's
  data sheet, finite-difference derivatives, and the ``urchin`` URDF
  forward-kinematics engine.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - kinematics
  - inverse-kinematics
  - jacobian
  - trajectory-planning
  - kuka
  - manipulator
  - denavit-hartenberg
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-04-29"
